; =============================================================================
; MUSIC STYLIST PRESET RECORDS (StyleRec_000 .. StyleRec_999)
; =============================================================================
; ROM range 0x951000-0x983B39.  This is the MUSIC STYLIST preset database:
; 1000 records of 198 bytes in a contiguous grid - 250 styles x 4 arrangement
; variations, grouped into the ten Stylist categories (the firmware's own
; help text: "Explore 1000 Musical Styles with the Music Stylist."):
;
;   records 000-123  Easy Listening    (31 styles)
;   records 124-255  Rock & Pop        (33 styles)
;   records 256-323  Dance Pop         (17 styles)
;   records 324-399  Party Music       (19 styles)
;   records 400-471  Gospel/Blues/R&B  (18 styles)
;   records 472-591  Jazz & Swing      (30 styles)
;   records 592-715  Show/Trad Dance   (31 styles)
;   records 716-815  Trad & Folk       (25 styles)
;   records 816-883  Country           (17 styles)
;   records 884-999  Latin / World     (29 styles)
;
; No code addresses the records directly: maincpu reaches them exclusively
; through the two 1000-entry pointer tables at 0x986000/0x987000
; (StyleRec_PtrTable_C2C5 / StyleRec_PtrTable_Default, see
; style_record_ptr_tables.s), selected on the CURRENT UI STATE ID in RAM
; 0x8D38 - NOT a model code as previously documented.
;
; RECORD LAYOUT (grid stride 198 = the 197 bytes the size field declares
; + 1 uncommitted pad byte; consumers cited from v10 ui/ui_mode_handlers.s,
; same code in v7/v9):
;   +0x00  .long 197   record byte count
;   +0x04  .long 77    offset to the parameter block
;                      (EffectMode_ClampAndLookupPreset: add xhl, (xwa + 4))
;   +0x08  16-char space-padded category name  ("Easy Listening")
;   +0x18  16-char space-padded style name     ("German Schlager")
;   +0x28  .short 1    constant in all 1000 records
;   +0x2a  .byte 32    display-string length: MssName_EventDispatch does
;                      Strncpy(dst, rec+43, rec[42])
;   +0x2b  32-char display string = 29-char arrangement name + 3-char
;          right-aligned ASCII tempo (EffectMode_DisplayPresetName copies
;          only its first 16 chars for the narrow name box)
;   +0x4b  .byte 0, 0  NUL terminator (+ pad) for the display string
;   +0x4d  113-byte PARAMETER BLOCK (+0x4d..+0xbd): the panel setup the
;          Stylist applies -- DECODED 2026-09-25, see "PARAMETER BLOCK"
;          below.  CORRECTED: this line used to read "115-byte parameter
;          block ... MIDI-range values, undecoded"; the reader stops at 113,
;          and the other two bytes are +0xbe and the first 0xff of the fill.
;   +0xbe  1 byte that none of the three readers below applies: 0x40 x850,
;          0xad x95, 0x97 x54, 0x99 x1.  Searched for: every reader of the
;          two pointer tables (5 code sites in v10, listed in
;          style_record_ptr_tables.s) and every reader of the block pointer
;          RAM 0x8D60 (one: EffectMode_UpdateBitFlags) -- no reader found.
;   +0xbf  6 x 0xff    constant fill in all 1000 records (+0xbf..+0xc4;
;          CORRECTED from "+0xc0 5 x 0xff", which left +0xbf in the block)
;   +0xc5  1 uncommitted grid pad byte (assorted leftover values; preserved
;          verbatim, NOT part of the 197-byte record)
;
; After the grid, 0x981570-0x983B39 is UNREFERENCED RESIDUE (no pointer into it
; exists in any program ROM: v7, v9 or v10).
;
; IDENTIFIED 2026-08-21, correcting the guess this comment used to record.  It
; is not "an older generation of this flash region" and not a discarded
; predecessor: 0x98156F-0x985FFF is a BYTE-IDENTICAL COPY OF THE LIVE HELP
; DATABASE REGION 0x98956F-0x98DFFF, written exactly 0x8000 (32 KB) lower.  A
; single byte differs in the whole 18 KB, at 0x983B39 (0x44 here, 0x20 in the
; live copy), and that byte is the pad between the two streams.
;
; So the two "residues" are one object seen in two halves: 0x98156F-0x983B38
; is the tail of the ENGLISH help database and 0x983B3A-0x985FFF is the GERMAN
; one, truncated at 0x986000 by the Music Stylist pointer tables.  The "LZSS
; text shreds" are exactly that -- SLIDE8K output -- and the "ramp" is not a
; separate family of data but ordinary back-references whose ring offsets climb
; linearly through band A.
;
; Reproduce: scripts/analysis/verify_stale_band.py original_ROMs/kn5000_table_data.rom
;
; PARAMETER BLOCK -- WHERE EVERY BYTE GOES (read from the code 2026-09-25)
; The block is applied to the live panel TLV stream at maincpu RAM 0xF9A0
; (records [tag][len][payload], schema in ROM at 0xED8FE0; see
; analysis/disk-format-probes/README-lsw-panel-schema.md), through its
; mirror at RAM 0x03C2C4, by three readers.  Addresses are v10 = v9 [v7]:
;   EffectMode_ClampAndLookupPreset 0xFB6DAB [0xFB65EA] returns the block,
;       rec + LE32 rec[+4] = rec + 77; EffectMode_ProcessPresetChange stores
;       it at RAM 0x8D60.
;   EffectMode_UpdateBitFlags 0xFB6EEA [0xFB6729] walks the table
;       WidgetStyleDataTable_0x2A8 (0xEB7BDA in all three): 30 entries of
;       {u32 panel offset from 0xF9A0, u8 sub-offset, u8 count}, ended by
;       u32 0xFF, copying parameter bytes 0..112 in order.  That table IS
;       the record layout, and it is what pins the block at 113 bytes.
;   BitMapOut_ByteData_PatchTable 0xFB63DC [0xFB5C1B], the unrolled variant
;       EffectMode_UpdateDisplay calls instead when RAM 0x8D52 bit 5 is set:
;       the same destination for each of the 98 bytes it copies, some under
;       a mask (listed below).  It skips bytes 6/16/26 (part +6), 29..33
;       (part 03) and 68..71/73..75 (style number, tag 48 +2/+3/+7, tempo),
;       so that path leaves the current style and tempo alone.
;   EffectMode_CopyVoiceParams 0xFB69EA [0xFB6229] runs after either, and
;       only when tag 70 +3 == 3 copies bytes 29..33 into part 03 at +0, +1,
;       +3, +4 (& 0xcf) and +8.  The walker table sends 29/30 to part 03
;       +1/+2 instead: the two readers DISAGREE on those two bytes.  That is
;       recorded here, not resolved.
; v10, v9 and v7 carry the identical table and identical routine bodies.
;
;   rec    n   destination                     what it is
;   +0x4d  10  part 00 +0..+9    RIGHT 1       part payload: +0 sound (program)
;   +0x57  10  part 01 +0..+9    RIGHT 2       +1 bank, +2 = 0 in all 1000, +3 a
;   +0x61   9  part 02 +0..+8    LEFT          level [I], +4 bit 6 reverb on,
;                                              bit 3 chorus on (PatchTable keeps
;                                              the live bits 5:4), +6 = 0 in all
;                                              1000, +7 a level [I], +8 pan [I]
;   +0x6a   5  part 03 (see above) sound, bank, +3, +4, +8
;   +0x6f  10  parts 10..14 +3, +7  ACC1 ACC2 ACC3 RHYTHM BASS
;   +0x79   8  tag 44 +0..+7     RIGHT 1 drawbar registration
;   +0x81   8  tag 45 +0..+7     RIGHT 2 drawbar registration
;   +0x89   8  tag 46 +0..+7     LEFT drawbar registration: +3..+7 low/high
;              nibbles = 16'/8', 5 1/3'/4', 2 2/3'/2', 1 3/5'/1 1/3', 1'; the
;              row comment prints them in footage order 16' 5 1/3' 8' 4' ...
;   +0x91   2  tag 48 +0/+1      STYLE NUMBER (11-bit, the word
;              AccHelper_ComputeVoiceOffset reads at 0xFC5A)
;   +0x93   3  tag 48 +2, +3, +4 +2 = 0 and +3 = 0xea in all 1000; the
;              PatchTable path applies only bit 6 of +4
;   +0x96   1  tag 48 +7         bits 5:4 = record index mod 4 in 998 of 1000
;              (not records 321 and 921): the arrangement's slot in its style
;   +0x97   2  tag 48 +8/+9      TEMPO in BPM (the word SeqTimer_PostTempoUpdate
;              stores at 0xFC62); equals the display-string tempo in 991 of
;              1000 -- 99, 379, 538, 710, 711, 734, 865, 978, 979 differ by 1-5
;   +0x99   4  tag 90 +0..+3     PatchTable masks 0x1f, 0x1f, 0xff, 0x01
;   +0x9d   1  tag 60 +1         PatchTable takes bits 7:6 only
;   +0x9e  18  tag 61 +0..+17    DSP-effect slot-0 block (DSPCfg_InitAllEntries
;              hands tag 61 to DSPCfg_WriteAllSlots_Combined as slot 0)
;   +0xb0   9  tag 63 +0..+8     the block ReverbPreset_Load sends [I: reverb]
;   +0xb9   2  tag 65 +0, +1     DSP-effect slot 2 block
;   +0xbb   3  tag 70 +0, +3, +4 digital-effect selection (PatchTable masks
;              0x04, 0xff, 0x0f)
; Part names: tags 00/01/02 = RIGHT 1/RIGHT 2/LEFT (part-name table 0xE9F374
; and the drawbar records' own part index); 10..14 = ACC1/ACC2/ACC3/RHYTHM/
; BASS after the AccPatch_UpdateChain_* routines.  What each panel field
; means, with its evidence and grade, is in analysis/disk-format-probes/
; README-lsw-part-record-fields.md, README-lsw-nonpart-records.md and
; README-lsw-drawbar-records.md; [I] marks what those notes grade inference.
; Part 03 is "PART 4" at index 3 of the part-name table 0xE9F374 (indices
; 0/1/2 are RIGHT1/RIGHT2/LEFT); which panel part that is on the instrument is
; not established here.
; The style number is constant within a style name except "German Schlager",
; which is two styles (90 and 1400) sharing one name.
; Reproduce every number in this header:
;   python3 notes/tonedb-2026-09-25/style_record_field_map.py
;
; Generated by scripts/generators/gen_style_records.py; this file is the
; authoritative source.
; The parameter-block rows and the two-line header above each record were
; re-emitted from the ROM bytes by scripts/tools/style_records_field_rows.py
; (2026-09-25).
; =============================================================================

	.org 0x951000 - 0x800000, 0xff

